            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"}> supergravity
            ), the divergence appears only in higher
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+order"} loop order
          %p That it appears earliest at 3-loops was established in
          %ul
            %li
              %p M. T. Grisaru, Phys. Lett. B 66, 75 (1977);
            %li
              %p E. T. Tomboulis, Phys. Lett. B67, 417 (1977);
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Deser"}> Stanley Deser
                , J. H. Kay and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"} Kellogg Stelle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Renata+Kallosh"}> Renata Kallosh
                , Phys. Lett. B99, 122 (1981);
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"}> Paul Howe
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"} Kellogg Stelle
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
          %p
            Specifically for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D8+d%3D4+supergravity"} N=8 d=4 supergravity
            there is evidence that it might be finite at all loops. See the references
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "4-dimensional+supergravity#PerturbativeQuantumSupergravityN8"} there
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              Assaf Shomer:
              %em A pedagogical explanation for the non-renormalizability of gravity
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0709.3555"}> arXiv:0709.3555
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/761598"} spire:761598
          %h3#from_string_field_theory From string field theory
          %p
            Derivation of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graviton"} graviton
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitudes"} scattering amplitudes
            from
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+field+theory"} string field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taejin+Lee"}> Taejin Lee
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gravitational Scattering Amplitudes and Closed String Field Theory in the Proper-Time Gauge
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1051/epjconf/201816807004"} doi:10.1051/epjconf/201816807004
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taejin+Lee"}> Taejin Lee
                ,
                %em Four-Graviton Scattering and String Path Integral in the Proper-time gauge
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.02702"}> arXiv:1806.02702
                )
          %h3#local_gauging_of_global_symmetries Local Gauging of global symmetries
          %p
            It is being argued that after embedding into consistent
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+symmetries"} global symmetries
            must become
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+symmetries"} local symmetries
          %p
            A substantiation of this argument via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} AdS/CFT
            is given in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Harlow"}> Daniel Harlow
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirosi+Ooguri"} Hirosi Ooguri
                %em Symmetries in quantum field theory and quantum gravity
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.05338"}> arXiv:1810.05338
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Harlow"}> Daniel Harlow
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirosi+Ooguri"} Hirosi Ooguri
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Constraints on symmetry from holography
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.05337"} arXiv:1810.05337
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Sylvain Fichet, Prashant Saraswat,
              %em Approximate Symmetries and Gravity
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.02002"}> arXiv:1909.02002
              )
          %div
            %h3#3dGravityAndChernSimonsTheoryReferences 3d Gravity and Chern-Simons theory
            %p
              On 3-dimensional (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"}> quantum
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+relativity"}> general relativity
              ) with
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
              with non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+groups"} gauge groups
            %p
              The original articles on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d+gravity"} 3d gravity
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
              and discovering its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holography"} holographic
              relation to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
              (well before
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} AdS/CFT
              was conceived from
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Deser"}> Stanley Deser
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roman+Jackiw"} Roman Jackiw
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerard+%27t+Hooft"} Gerard 't Hooft
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Three-dimensional Einstein gravity: Dynamics of flat space
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0003-4916(84)90085-X"} doi:10.1016/0003-4916(84)90085-X
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Deser"}> Stanley Deser
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roman+Jackiw"} Roman Jackiw
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Three-dimensional cosmological gravity: Dynamics of constant curvature
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0003-4916(84)90025-3"} doi:10.1016/0003-4916(84)90025-3
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/192694"} spire:192694
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roman+Jackiw"}> Roman Jackiw
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Lower dimensional gravity
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(85)90448-1"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(85)90448-1
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/204694"} spire:204694
              %li
                %p
                  J. D. Brown,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Henneaux"} Marc Henneaux
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Central charges in the canonical realization of asymptotic symmetries: An example from three dimensional gravity
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01211590"} doi:10.1007/BF01211590
              %li
                %p
                  A. Achucarro,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em A Chern-Simons Action for Three-Dimensional anti-De Sitter Supergravity Theories
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(86)90140-1"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(86)90140-1
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/21208"} spire:21208
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Carlip"}> Steven Carlip
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Inducing Liouville theory from topologically massive gravity
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(91)90558-F"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(91)90558-F
              %li
                %p
                  O. Coussaert,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Henneaux"} Marc Henneaux
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The asymptotic dynamics of three-dimensional Einstein gravity with a negative cosmological constant
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9506019"} arXiv:gr-qc/9506019
            %p
              The corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+QFT"} non-perturbative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
              of 3-dimensional gravity, via
              = succeed ":" do
